n  1025→        ``falcon.MEDIA_XML``, ``falcon.MEDIA_HTML``,\n  1026→        ``falcon.MEDIA_JS``, ``falcon.MEDIA_TEXT``,\n  1027→        ``falcon.MEDIA_JPEG``, ``falcon.MEDIA_PNG``,\n  1028→        and ``falcon.MEDIA_GIF``.\n  1029→        \"\"\",\n  1030→    )\n  1031→\n  1032→    downloadable_as = header_property(\n  1033→        'Content-Disposition',\n  1034→        \"\"\"Set the Content-Disposition header using the given filename.\n  1035→\n  1036→        The value will be used for the ``filename`` directive. For example,\n  1037→        given ``'report.pdf'``, the Content-Disposition header would be set\n  1038→        to: ``'attachment; filename=\"report.pdf\"'``.\n  1039→\n  1040→        As per `RFC 6266 <https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc6266#appendix-D>`_\n  1041→        recommendations, non-ASCII filenames will be encoded using the\n  1042→        ``filename*`` directive, whereas ``filename`` will contain the US\n  1043→        ASCII fallback.\n  1044→        \"\"\",\n  1045→        functools.partial(format_content_disposition, disposition_type='attachment'),\n  1046→    )\n  1047→\n  1048→    viewable_as = header_property(\n  1049→        'Content-Disposition',\n  1050→        \"\"\"Set an inline Content-Disposition header using the given filename.\n  1051→\n  1052→        The value will be used for the ``filename`` directive. For example,\n  1053→        given ``'report.pdf'``, the Content-Disposition header would be set\n  1054→        to: ``'inline; filename=\"report.pdf\"'``.\n  1055→\n  1056→        As per `RFC 6266 <https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc6266#appendix-D>`_\n  1057→        recommendations, non-ASCII filenames will be encoded using the\n  1058→        ``filename*`` directive, whereas ``filename`` will contain the US\n  1059→        ASCII fallback.\n  1060→\n  1061→        .. versionadded:: 3.1\n  1062→        \"\"\",\n  1063→        functools.partial(format_content_disposition, disposition_type='inline'),\n  1064→    )\n  1065→\n  1066→    etag